    "blurb": "The show shines with a blistering Truckin' → Dark Star → Morning Dew sequence and an inspired China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue. Box of Rain, Playing In The Band and Sugar Magnolia also stand out. Overall the performance is high‑energy with strong improvisational flow.",
    "review": "December 15, 1972 at Long Beach Arena finds the Dead on the cusp of their 1973 breakthrough, delivering a set that crackles from start to finish. After a loose first half the band really clicks on the second set, launching into a spectacular Truckin' → Dark Star → Morning Dew journey where Jerry’s wha‑wha guitar licks and Santana‑style bends weave through Keith’s atonal, Miles‑Davis‑like keyboard runs. Phil’s “cool” bass notes and occasional squeaks push the jam into psychedelic overdrive, while Bill’s drumming settles into a solid groove that supports the soaring improvisations. The first set offers classic moments too – a seamless China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider transition, a heartfelt Box of Rain, and an expansive 18‑minute Playing In The Band that hints at the band’s upcoming exploratory direction. With high‑energy delivery and tight interplay, this show is a must‑listen for anyone tracking the Dead’s evolution toward their early‑’70s zenith.",
